meta {
  name: Phase 5 - Final Clearance
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/seat-cancellations/{{seatCancellationId}}/final-clearance
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "refund_transaction_ref": "REF-2023-892-01",
    "refund_payment_method": "Bank Transfer (Bank of India)"
  }
}

docs {
  Marks documents handed over and finalizes the case. This is where the
  real side effects fire (same ones the old one-shot "approve" review used
  to trigger), inside one transaction:
  - Enrollment.status -> "withdrawn"
  - ApplicationCourse.status -> "dropped_out" (+ status log entry)
  - Seat released back to the course quota / seat pool
  - Student's BeaconU Card deactivated
  - SeatCancellation.status -> "approved"

  refund_transaction_ref / refund_payment_method: REQUIRED only when the
  case's settlement was Case B (Refund Eligible) — manual bookkeeping
  fields, staff types in whatever reference/method they used for the actual
  bank transfer. Not sent/used for Case A or C.

  409 ConflictError if the case isn't currently at Phase 5, or (Case B) if
  refund_transaction_ref is missing.
}
